Package: kioto
Title: Lock-Free Shared-Memory Channels and Task Pools
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Charlie", "Gao", , "charlie.gao@posit.co", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0750-061X")),
    person("Posit Software, PBC", role = c("cph", "fnd"),
           comment = c(ROR = "03wc8by49")),
    person("Pierre", "L'Ecuyer", role = "cph",
           comment = "RngStreams library")
  )
Description: Parallel computation and data exchange between R processes on
    the same machine: lock-free channels and work-stealing task pools over
    'POSIX' shared memory (Linux, macOS) or 'Win32' file mappings
    (Windows), with the hot path entirely in user space. Inter-process
    communication cheap enough that work can be divided at granularities
    usually reserved for threads. A complement to 'mirai'; payload
    contents interoperate transparently with 'mori' shared objects.
